  "goal": "Close the source-local routine recovery and verified-reuse dependency chain by binding every executed or reused downstream row to the exact selected upstream result artifact, replacing timing-based interruption with a bounded readiness handshake, and exercising clean, dirty, conflict, fallback, repeat-use, mutation, refusal, and zero-write journeys.",
  "success": [
    "Every executed or reused report row is reconciled in two passes against the exact selected upstream result artifact digest and behaviorally passed disposition.",
    "Same-plan substitution, missing, failed, duplicate, unknown, reordered, stale, and mutation-forced dependency chains fail closed without converting proxy evidence into acceptance.",
    "Process interruption uses an exact bounded readiness handshake and independently proves interrupt-before-readiness without assuming a child process record exists.",
    "Clean no-op, dirty dependency-closed, conflict-strict, optional fallback, first execution, exact repeat reuse, and mutation-forced miss journeys preserve unrelated bytes and zero-write read/refusal behavior.",
    "Correction controls, journey target, and the expanded dependency-closed routine surface pass twice without retries under the isolated offline 16-thread target.",
    "The self-excluded WorkerResult binds every worker-owned artifact and preserves the no-claim ceiling for public command behavior, cross-platform recovery, live product journeys, node closure, readiness, release, and completion."
  ],
